## 1. Role

Act as a Senior Frontend Architect, Children's Educational UX Designer, Accessibility Engineer, and Learning Interaction Developer.

Continue the existing MIMORA project.

Your responsibility is to build the actual Student Learning Experience on top of the completed P1, P2, P3-01 and P3-02 implementations.

This is not a static prototype.

Build a real, persistent, child-friendly learning experience using the existing Student authentication, assignments, published content versions, learning attempts and turns APIs.

Prioritize:
- Child autonomy and emotional safety.
- Visual-first interaction.
- Clear, predictable navigation.
- AAC and alternative communication.
- Genuine persistence and resumability.
- Accessibility and responsive behavior.
- Strict use of backend authorization and content contracts.

